(35, 1, '2020-01-09 09:34:28', '2020-01-09 09:34:28', '<strong>Shri Ram Rural Welfare Educational Society\'s</strong> work is concentrated in the fields of Education, Health, and Community Development which we believe are the areas of greatest need and deserve to be the foci of our attention. We believe the three are inter-related fields and together the only way to make a sustainable and impactful difference in the beneficial population. We work for the upliftment of the poor and destitute by helping them achieve social-economic independence. Self-sustainability and health. We do everything from providing educational and health services to the needy mainstreaming marginalized urban and rural people, making low-literate youth employable, and employing women.\r\n\r\nThe Society has been conceived to Impart World-class education in the Medical/ Allied Sciences, to manage and open Charitable Hospital/Diagnostic Centers, holding free Medical camps, giving scholarships to poor needy students, and to provide help to persons affected by natural calamities like earthquake, flood, etc.\r\n\r\nIn-country alike India where there is a high rate of unemployment, these courses are designed to provide immediate employment to the candidates. The Secretary Dr. N.K. Pandey is an MD of M/S Shri Ram M.R.I. Scan Center. Based at Siwan. He Travels abroad frequently and Understands that the employment avenues are growing globally for Paramedical Personnel. The Society unlike other Institutes in India has its own equipment like MRI, CT Scan, Color Doppler, Digital X-Ray, OPG, EEG, ECG, TMT, PFT, Mammography, Lithotripsy, and well equipped Medical Lab For Practical training of its Students. Society is affiliated with Bihar State Government &amp; AICT Approved.\r\n\r\n<strong>Managing Committee :</strong>\r\n<strong>President</strong> Dr. Chandra Shekhar Mishra\r\n\r\n<strong> Secretary</strong> Dr. Naval Kishor Pandey\r\n\r\n<strong>Treasurer</strong> Pragya\r\n\r\n<strong>Members</strong>\r\n\r\nDr. Suneshwar Kumar Singh\r\n\r\nDr. Taufique Ahmad\r\n\r\nSri Gorakh Mishra\r\n\r\nSri Lalan Tiwari\r\n\r\nSri Rajesh Kumar Ojha\r\n\r\nSri Prakash Pandey\r\n\r\nSmt. Usha Devi\r\n\r\n<strong>Principal</strong>\r\n\r\nDr. J.N.Prasad\r\n\r\n<strong>Vice Principal\r\n</strong>Dr. Astha', 'About Orgnization', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'about-orgnization', '', '', '2025-11-15 11:29:22', '2025-11-15 11:29:22', '', 0, 'http://srioms.co.in/?p=35', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(36, 1, '2020-01-09 09:34:28', '2020-01-09 09:34:28', 'The Society has been conceived to Impart World class education in the Medical/ Allied Sciences, to manage and open Charitable Hospital/Diagnostic Centers, holding free Medical camps, giving scholarship to poor needy students and to provide help to persons affected by natural calamities like earthquake, flood etc.\r\n\r\nIn country like India where there is a high rate of unemployment these courses are designed to provide immediate employment to the candidates. The Secretary Dr. N.K. Pandey ia a MD of M/S Shri Ram M.R.I. Scan Center. Based at Siwan. He Travels abroad frequently and Understands that the employment avenues are growing globally for Paramedical Personnel’s. The Society unlike other Institutes in India has its own Equipments like MRI, CT Scan, Color Doppler, Digital X-Ray, OPG, EEG, ECG, TMT,PFT, Mammography, Lithotripsy and well equipped Medical Lab For Practical training of its Students. Society is affiliated with Bihar State Government &amp; AICT Approved.', 'About Orgnization', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '35-revision-v1', '', '', '2020-01-09 09:34:28', '2020-01-09 09:34:28', '', 35, 'http://srioms.co.in/index.php/2020/01/09/35-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
